		<div class="texto-blog">					
		<p>We will learn in this <strong>CodeIgniter 4 course/tutorial from scratch</strong>, how to install with composer, the operation of the controllers, views, routes, everything step by step.</p>

		<h2>How to install CodeIgniter 4 with composer?</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }}

		<p>First we need to have installed on our computer <strong>php</strong> from its version <strong>7.3</strong> henceforth, have the extensions enabled <strong>intl/mbstring</strong>, and <a class="text-info" href="https://getcomposer.org/" target="_blank">Composer</a> for handling dependencies, first we run the following command to create a new project.</p>

		<code>composer create-project codeigniter4/appstarter tutorial-ci4</code>		

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/tutorial-ci41.png" alt="ci41">

		</div>

		<p>Then we will list and give all the permissions to our project which is called <strong>tutorial-ci4</strong>.</p>
			

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/tutorial-ci42.png" alt="ci42">

		</div>

		<p>We navigate to the interior of our project, with which we will find ourselves in the root and we will start the development server, we will use the <strong>command line tool</strong>.</p>

		<code>php spark serve</code>	
			

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/tutorial-ci43.png" alt="ci43">

		</div>

		<p>We copy the url in our browser, with which we have the project running.</p>			

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/tutorial-ci44.png" alt="ci44">

		</div>

		<p>We will create a new file called <code>.env</code> to add the environment variables, we will modify the variables <code>CI_ENVIRONMENT</code> and <code>app.baseURL</code>, to work in a state of development.</p>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
	#--------------------------------------------------------------------
	# Example Environment Configuration file
	#
	# This file can be used as a starting point for your own
	# custom .env files, and contains most of the possible settings
	# available in a default install.
	#
	# By default, all of the settings are commented out. If you want
	# to override the setting, you must un-comment it by removing the '#'
	# at the beginning of the line.
	#--------------------------------------------------------------------

	#--------------------------------------------------------------------
	# ENVIRONMENT
	#--------------------------------------------------------------------

	  CI_ENVIRONMENT = development

	#--------------------------------------------------------------------
	# APP
	#--------------------------------------------------------------------

	  app.baseURL = 'http://localhost:8080/'
		</code>
		</pre>


		<p>We will create a new controller, if you want to know how the default controller works read the following article <a class="text-info" href="/codeigniter-4-controllers">CodeIgniter 4 Controllers</a>.</p>

		<code>php spark make:controller Student</code>				

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/tutorial-ci45.png" alt="ci45">

		</div>

		<p>We will create a new route in <code>nameProject/app/Config/Routes.php</code>, with which we associate a url, the class and the name of the method.</p>

		<code>$routes->get('/student', 'Student::index');</code>

		<p>We verify the set of routes that we have created.</p>

		<code>php spark routes</code>						

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/tutorial-ci46.png" alt="ci46">

		</div>

